Chapter: PondSpec
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Safari chapter Pond
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 Pond: pure data, spot-checked, plus the one thing its prose claims and nothing
 verifies.

 THE VALUES ARE THE ART AND THEY ARE PINNED, NOT DERIVED. There is no arithmetic
 here to work out an answer from: a pond outline is a shape somebody drew, and
 the oracle for whether it is the RIGHT shape is PondCheck against the zig probe,
 which reads the game module itself. This file asks a different and cheaper
 question -- does the chapter compile, load, and still hold what it held -- and a
 spot check answers it. Grading all nineteen points would not answer it any
 better.

 THE INVARIANT IS THE PART THAT IS NOT A PIN. The chapter says the ducks sit
 "inside the outline", and nothing checks it. The water spans cu -31 to -1 and cv
 3 to 32, so every duck must fall inside that box -- a weaker claim than being
 inside the polygon, and still one that catches a duck moved out onto the grass
 or a sign flipped on a cu. It is derived from the outline rather than from the
 duck list, so the two have to agree for it to pass.

 THE FRAME, SO THE SIGNS READ: cv is metres BEYOND the incoming segment's end
 edge and cu is metres across from its end-left corner, positive toward the road.
 The pond is off to the LEFT, which is why every cu here is negative.

 We say:

Section: Sizes And Colours

  size-got : List Integer
  size-got = [list-length water-outline, list-length bank, list-length ducks, water-color, bank-color, duck-codepoint]

  size-want : List Integer
  size-want = [7, 6, 6, 3112588, 12759680, 129414]

Section: Spot Points

 The outline's near edge at cv 3, its far tip, the bank's first point, and the
 duck height -- one value from each binding in the chapter.

  spot-got : List Real
  spot-got = [(list-at water-outline 0).cu, (list-at water-outline 0).cv, (list-at water-outline 4).cu, (list-at water-outline 4).cv, (list-at bank 0).cu, (list-at bank 0).cv, duck-height]

  spot-want : List Real
  spot-want = [-2.0, 3.0, -15.0, 32.0, -5.0, 29.0, 0.9]

Section: The Ducks Are On The Water

 Written as nested ifs rather than a conjunction so that nothing here depends on
 which spelling of `and` an arm accepts; this file is partly a front-end check
 and should not import a question it is not asking.

  inside : Duck -> Boolean
  inside (d) =
    if d.p.cu > -1.0 then False
    else if d.p.cu < -31.0 then False
    else if d.p.cv < 3.0 then False
    else if d.p.cv > 32.0 then False
    else True

  inside-got : List Boolean
  inside-got = list-map inside ducks

  inside-want : List Boolean
  inside-want = [True, True, True, True, True, True]

 The six face-right flags, which alternate in no pattern and so are the one part
 of the duck table a careless regeneration would silently normalise.

  face-got : List Boolean
  face-got = [(list-at ducks 0).face-right, (list-at ducks 1).face-right, (list-at ducks 2).face-right, (list-at ducks 3).face-right, (list-at ducks 4).face-right, (list-at ducks 5).face-right]

  face-want : List Boolean
  face-want = [True, False, True, True, False, True]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "pd-size" size-got size-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "pd-spot" spot-got spot-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "pd-in  " inside-got inside-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "pd-face" face-got face-want)
  end
